           lost Kasper's comment 100% of the time it fired, whereas the
           clobber needs a second person editing the same card's scalars
           inside the same ~1s window. Do not restate this as "concurrent
           edits still conflict" -- an earlier draft of this comment did, and
           it is not what the code does.

           COMMENTS ARE NOT COVERED BY THAT TRADE AND MUST NOT BE. The one
           `comments_base_at` field drives calendar-upsert's scalar guard AND
           its per-cell comment merge, which keeps an existing comment missing
           from the incoming list only while that comment is NEWER than the
           baseline. Advancing the baseline to the bridge's stamp therefore
